<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guinea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guinea is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> that was part of French West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>. In 1958, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-sekou-toure">Sékou Touré</a>, it rejected de Gaulle's proposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-community">French Community</a> and chose immediate independence. This decision helped trigger the rapid dissolution of French colonial administration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sub-saharan-africa">sub-Saharan Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guinea.jpg" alt="Guinea" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Guinea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
